      "text": [
        ": \"دِيَةُ اَلْيَدِ إِذَا قُطِعَتْ خَمْسُونَ مِنَ اَلْإِبِلِ فَمَا كَانَ جُرُوحاً دُونَ اَلاِصْطِلاَمِ فَيَحْكُمُ بِهِ ذَوَا عَدْلٍ مِنْكُمْ \"وَ مَنْ لَمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمٰا أَنْزَلَ اَللّٰهُ فَأُولٰئِكَ هُمُ اَلْكٰافِرُونَ\" \""
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5279 - Ibn Al-Mughira narrated from Abdullah ibn Sinan from Abu Abdullah (as) who said: \"The blood money (diyya) for a hand if it is cut off is fifty camels.\nAs for wounds that are less severe than complete amputation, a ruling shall be made concerning them by two just individuals among you.\nAnd whoever does not judge by what Allah (swt) has revealed, then they are the disbelievers.\""
        ]
      }
